  "status": "SUCCESS",
  "summary": "All checks pass (lint clean, 145 tests pass, build OK).\n\n**What I changed**\n\n*6. Template File Upload (UC3)* — `TemplateEditor.jsx` now has a **Template File** picker (shown only to users who can manage templates, i.e. Tenant Admin / Legal Reviewer, which the page already gates). It accepts PDF/DOCX up to 25 MB and sets Document Format from the picked file; anything else is blocked with exactly `Unsupported file format. Please upload a PDF or DOCX file.` (and the existing 25 MB message for oversized files). Storing the file itself is backend work — the module contract has no template-file endpoint/field, so I did not invent a payload for it.\n\n*15. Thresholds and approval rules (UC10/UC11)* —\n- `BottleneckTab` gained an **Edit Thresholds** panel for Tenant Admins: per-stage day inputs validated as positive numbers only, saved via a new `updateBottleneckThresholds` (`PUT /api/v1/tracker/bottleneck-thresholds`) in `trackerService`/`useBottleneckThresholds`, after which the tab refetches so the Stuck Flag updates immediately.\n- Approval rules are now editable and deletable: `updateApprovalRule` (`PUT .../approval-rules/{id}`) and `deleteApprovalRule` (`DELETE .../approval-rules/{id}`) in `settingsApprovalRulesService`, new `useUpdateApprovalRule` / `useDeleteApprovalRule` hooks, Edit/Delete row actions in `RoutingApprovalTab`, and `AddRuleForm` reused in edit mode. Blank fields are blocked client-side; duplicate Contract Type + Value Threshold is blocked client-side (excluding the rule being edited) and still surfaces the server's message.\n\nLeft for the backend repository: the template-file storage endpoint, `PUT /api/v1/tracker/bottleneck-thresholds`, `PUT`/`DELETE /api/v1/settings/approval-rules/{ruleId}`, and the guarantee that deleting a rule leaves in-progress approvals untouched.",
